Phase 6 — CUDA Barnes–Hut 🔥

Now comes the difficult part.

GPU implementation of Barnes–Hut is harder because tree algorithms are irregular.

You'll need to investigate:

Particle data
     ↓
Tree construction
     ↓
Tree representation
     ↓
GPU traversal
     ↓
Force calculation

Potential approaches:

Approach A — CPU tree + GPU force calculation
CPU
 ↓
Build tree
 ↓
GPU
 ↓
Traverse tree + calculate forces

Start here.

Much easier.

Approach B — GPU tree construction

Later:

GPU
 ↓
Build tree
 ↓
GPU traversal
 ↓
GPU force calculation

This is much harder, but potentially much more impressive.

Phase 7 — GPU Optimization

Once the CUDA version works, don't immediately optimize everything.

Profile it first.

Investigate:

global memory accesses
shared memory
occupancy
branch divergence
memory transfer overhead
kernel execution time
tree traversal cost

Use NVIDIA tools such as:

Nsight Systems
Nsight Compute

Then optimize one bottleneck at a time.

Phase 8 — n-Dimensional Generalization

Only after the 2D/3D version works should you generalize.

Create something conceptually like:

Particle<Dim>

and:

BarnesHutTree<Dim>

Then experiment with:

2D
3D
4D
5D
...

The project title becomes much more interesting:

CUDA-Accelerated Barnes–Hut Simulation in Arbitrary Dimensions

But don't make n-dimensionality your first priority.

Correct + fast 3D > broken 10D.

